# Provenance of this corpus.
#
# Update this file each time you repin the plugin, so that the next repin can
# diff tag to tag.

repo     https://github.com/lukewilliamboswell/roc-ray
tag      0.10.0
platform 5xecDmRJroKT9fnSiYsGdCKEzNWLnRKGtHJ5CxuCnpb9.tar.zst
# The release's other bundle, DDs5HiQ8vfCk6zFwWshZ9Dyx3avmQqV9EuNkQn4VGmHi.tar.zst,
# is the Wayland build of the same platform. Its .roc modules have the same API.
# Nothing here pins it. There is no types bundle. In 0.10.0 the platform
# contains the roc-ray-types package of the release candidates, so this plugin
# has no types/ directory and the manifest has no `packages` entry.

# The nightly every app here was checked under, and the manifest's `compiler`
# line. It is the release's own "Supported compiler", and the platform bundle's
# header pins it with a `roc: "nightly-2026-09-27-a3ce7f1"` entry.
#
# Because of that pin, this is not the nightly in corpus/language/UPSTREAM. Under
# nightly-2026-10-04-130536d every app here fails the gate on exactly one
# diagnostic, a "roc version mismatch" warning pointing at the cached
# platform's main.roc:66, and the bundle is content-addressed, so nothing in
# this plugin can drop it. With that one line stripped from a local copy of the
# bundle (`roc check --replace-dep <bundle url> <copy>/main.roc`), every app
# here checks clean under 10-04 too. Moving this pin needs a roc-ray release
# whose bundle pins 10-04 or pins nothing.
compiler nightly-2026-09-27-a3ce7f1

index.json <- the release bundle's own .roc modules, parsed by
              `roc-syntax-mcp plugin index`. No source is vendored: the
              manifest names the bundle URL, and every app pins the same one
examples/  <- examples-0.10.0.zip, one directory per example, flattened to
              examples/<name>.roc
topics/    <- this package's own, not upstream's: programs written against
              this pin and declared in plugin.json so they answer by name
overview.md <- this package's own. Its setup, permission and shipping advice
              is drawn from the release notes and docs/*.adoc at this tag, and
              every API claim on it is compiled by verify/overview-snippets.roc

# What examples/ leaves out, and why. In a diff, an omitted example looks the
# same as a missing one, so this list names each omitted example:
#   breakout    imports sibling modules, and the gate compiles one file at a time
#   cave_climb  the same
#   snake       the same
#   top_down    the same
#   live_plot   statically imports a font file the compiler reads at check time
# breakout, snake and top_down were single files at 0.10.0-rc3. 0.10.0 split
# them into modules.

# What else the release has and this package does not ship:
#   docs/*.adoc  the RocRay manual. It is AsciiDoc, and this host serves only
#                Markdown from a `docs` directory, so to bundle it, this
#                package would have to convert it
#   roc-ray-manual-0.10.0.*, roc-ray-api-docs-0.10.0.zip  rendered copies of
#                the same manual and of the API this corpus indexes

# The repin changes every vendored app in one way. It removes the
# `roc: "nightly-2026-09-27-a3ce7f1"` entry from each header, single-line and
# multi-line alike. The entry names the same nightly as the manifest, so it is
# redundant here, and under any other nightly it would add a second mismatch
# warning per file. The release zip already pins the 0.10.0 bundle URL, so
# nothing else in any example changes.

# Parsed counts at this pin, for the next repin to diff against. These are what
# `plugin validate` reports on its `corpus` line:
